.SH DONE 2026\-08\-30: THE HUMAN CHANNEL MOVED TO CONTAINERS
This was a precondition nobody had written down. `wsl \-\-shutdown' used to cost
Zach's notification channel, which is why senechal#561's fix sat unapplied.
.PP
.B What was actually wrong.
The container stack was the intended design and it had been DOWN for 13 hours:
`zaxon\-gateway' exited 75 with `failed to bind host port 127.0.0.1:8090/tcp:
address already in use'. Because all distros share one netns, hermes's NATIVE
whisper\-server (:8090) and zaxon\-relay\-mcp (:8643) occupied the exact ports
the container anchor needed. Retiring hermes was not cleanup \- it was the fix.
.PP
.B The state was split\-brain, not stale.
Both stacks had been running and writing to separate directories since
2026\-08\-29 19:37. Resolved by asking which side was LIVE, not which mtime was
newer: the container side's last write was 08\-29 23:23; hermes wrote
continuously for the ~12h after. So hermes's lineage won wholesale \- with ONE
exception:
.nf

  hermes wins   state.db tickets.db kanban.db response_store.db
                whatsapp/session/ (2635 files) channel_directory cron logs
  container wins  .env  -- hermes's has 20 keys to the container's 19, and the
                  extra is HERMES_LOCAL_STT_COMMAND, which points at a NATIVE
                  whisper binary that does not exist inside a container
.fi
.PP
Backups on D:, kept: `hermes\-20260830.tar' (3.38G, full distro export),
`srv\-zaxon\-data\-before.tgz', `hermes\-final.tgz', `env\-container\-keep',
`wslconfig.bak\-20260830\-preexperimental'.
.PP
.B Verified after, and again after two wsl \-\-shutdown cycles:
MCP answers `"serverInfo":{"name":"zaxon"}', whisper `/health' ok, gateway
heartbeat advancing, FilmB 200/200. Everything came back UNATTENDED \-
docker.service is enabled and every container is `restart: always'. hermes did
not return: its four units are disabled AND masked, 0 .wants remaining.
.PP
.B autoMemoryReclaim is now in force
\- moved to [experimental] (senechal#561) and confirmed the only way that
mistake permits: by the ABSENCE of the `Unknown key' line on a real VM start.
.SH POST\-MIGRATION QUEUE
Parked deliberately until the cutover lands. Each carries the evidence it rests
on so the next agent does not re\-derive it.
.PP
.B 1. Uninstall Docker Desktop.
Installed, STOPPED, `AutoStart: false', zero processes, and no consumer found:
no ~/.docker on Ubuntu, no DOCKER_HOST anywhere, context `default',
/usr/bin/docker is the docker.io deb not a DD shim. ~13.6 GB, ALL on C: \- the
drive with ~52 GB free that also holds monkey's 39.5 GB rollback VDI.
FilmB, the only thing anyone wanted from it, was NEVER inside it: bind\-mounted
from C:\eUsers\eZach\eDocuments\eFilmB\eFilmBdb, so the 11 GB docker_data.vhdx
holds only re\-pullable images and build cache. Now migrated to /srv/filmb on
the native engine and verified \- 104/104 media URLs md5\-identical, DB
writable, integrity_check ok after SIGKILL.
Uninstalling also unregisters the `docker\-desktop' distro, removing its invalid
`automount.crossDistro' key and the trap where a bare `wsl \-d' starts it.
.B Set the default explicitly afterwards:
.nf

  wsl.exe \-\-set\-default Ubuntu
.fi
.PP
.B 2. wsl \-\-unregister hermes.
Export already taken. Its units are disabled and masked, its state migrated,
nothing on any host references it, and nothing starts it \- its 6d uptime was a
manual start, which is the unsupervised\-service failure dexter\-liveness.sh
exists for. Note `wsl \-\-export' STOPS the distro, and after it interop from
inside a distro breaks with `Exec format error'; drive it from port 22.
.PP
.B 3. etalon#22 \- the prose guard prices fenced comments and roff.
It closes two loopholes THIS FILE used: shell comments inside ``` fences in .md
were free, and roff was not priced at all. It recommends NOT exempting man/*
from the census, which correctly re\-prices this runbook. Draft, so its
DEFAULT\-AFTER clock is not running; mark it ready to queue the man/ question.
.PP
.B 4. dcp\-gate\-site standup.
Blocked on a runner that DOES NOT EXIST: `monkey\-dcp\-gate\-site' is registered
at GitHub but monkey carries 12 runner directories and none is this one. A
ghost registration, not a runner that fell over. Standing it up means
provisioning a 13th runner, which the migration re\-registers and which
realisateur#672 (decided) deletes in favour of one org\-level pool. The
`.agent\-project' marker landed separately (dcp\-gate\-site#97) because it needs
no runner and is the root cause: without it `registry\-standup.sh' does not list
the repo AT ALL, so no guard ever looked.
.SH RETIRING THIS
When etat.sh reports the cutover DONE and a week has passed with long_readout
at 0 \- so 2026\-09\-06 at the earliest \- delete this directory, the saved VM,
VirtualBox itself with nomac and crt\-vm, and D:\ewsl\-migration. Fold the
durable facts into bin/lib/vmhost.sh comments; leave nothing here to rot.
.PP
.B That window also carries the deferred disk move,
because it is the one moment C: has room and monkey is stopped anyway: shut WSL
down from port 22, move, start Ubuntu first and monkey second, restart the
runner units. Quiesce the runners before it \- stop, never deregister.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
constate.sh and etat.sh carry no comments on purpose: their reasoning is here,
in one document, rather than scattered across two scripts.
.PP
.B constate.sh
runs on mandark and reaches in. It is NOT a verb and is installed on no host,
so it needs no build tag to reach the thing it measures \- which matters,
because the verb build cuts only every 30 days. Its probe is one heredoc run
wherever \-\-target says. Every field exists because something downstream breaks
when it moves:
.nf

  MUST\-HOLD    machine_id hostname accounts crontabs etc_selfdev verbs_on_path
               and ts_ip / ts_nodeid \- what `Host monkey' and 12 runner
               registrations resolve through. ABSENT is expected on the
               rehearsal distro, which takes a fresh key on purpose; a SILENT
               change on the real cutover is the failure this exists to catch.
  MUST\-CHANGE  backend, oracle \-> wsl. The one field whose job is to flip.
  GRADED       runners_active may not fall; long_readout and soft_lockup may
               not rise.
.fi
.PP
A witness that cannot see exits 6 (BLIND) rather than reporting a clean, empty
pass \- "I could not look" reported as healthy is how ten days pass.
.PP
.B etat.sh
re\-derives the sprint's position from hosts and repos on every run; it reads no
box a human ticked. It always exits 0, so it can never redden CI or block a
turn. It checks the four vmhost wsl arms whose absence renders the published
status page permanently red, and it measures C: free against monkey.vdi \-
because rollback lives or dies on C: keeping that file.
